"Workflows for work that runs the business Mistral AI has unveiled 'Workflows', an orchestration layer with durability, observability, and fault tolerance for reliable operation and automation of enterprise AI processes. 'Workflows', an integrated orchestration layer for stable operation of AI models in an enterprise environment, has been released as a public preview. It provides the durability, observability, and fault tolerance essential for complex, multi-step business processes, enabling a smooth transition of AI processes to production. Developers create workflows in Python and manage them through Studio, and organization members can easily execute them through Le Chat. Speaking of Voxtral Mistral AI has launched 'Voxtral TTS', a lightweight 4B parameter scale text-to-speech (TTS) model with excellent multilingual speech generation performance. A lightweight model with 4B parameters, cost-effective for real-time large-scale voice agent services Supports 9 languages ​​and various dialects, and enables natural voice generation with excellent context understanding and emotional expression. Human evaluation results show that it provides more natural speech than ElevenLabs Flash v2.5 at a similar initial speech response rate (TTFA) and is of comparable quality to v3. Introducing Forge Mistral AI has unveiled 'Forge', a system that helps companies build cutting-edge AI models exclusively for companies by learning their own proprietary data. Forge enables the development of AI models specialized for domain knowledge by utilizing a company's internal documents, code base, and operational records. Through pre-learning, follow-up learning, and reinforcement learning, you can build AI agents that understand your company's unique workflows and policies and perform tasks. Enterprises can train models with their own infrastructure and data, retaining direct control over their intellectual property and data. Introducing Mistral Small 4 Mistral AI announced 'Mistral Small 4', a next-generation hybrid model that integrates reasoning, multimodal, and coding agent functions and significantly improves efficiency. Inference, multimodal, and coding capabilities are integrated into one model to maximize user convenience and versatility. Efficient task processing is possible by supporting MoE architecture consisting of 128 experts and 256k context windows. The new 'reasoning_effort' parameter allows you to dynamically adjust response speed and reasoning depth depending on the complexity of the task. Mistral AI partners with NVIDIA to accelerate open frontier models Mistral AI has decided to participate as a founding member of NVIDIA's 'Nemotron Coalition' to jointly develop open, cutting-edge AI models and expand the ecosystem. Mistral AI and NVIDIA join forces to jointly develop and optimize high-performance open source AI models Accelerate AI model development by combining Mistral AI’s model architecture with NVIDIA’s compute resources and development tools Enhancing technology accessibility and transparency through an open AI model that developers and companies can utilize The lawyer who won a $6 million verdict against Meta says AI let him do 30 hours of work in 10 We cover a case where a lawyer utilized AI tools to maximize work efficiency and achieve victory in a social media addiction lawsuit. Attorney Mark Lanier efficiently prepared for the lawsuit by reducing 30 hours of work to 10 hours using AI. During the trial, court records were analyzed every day with an AI model, which was used to evaluate jurors' questions and strengthen logical responses. Although AI is used for business analysis and efficient data organization, it has been cautious not to use it directly for legal document writing or unsupervised legal research. Skoda’s Peaq is a seven-seat electric SUV built to undercut the Kia EV9 and Ioniq 9 on price Skoda has unveiled 'Peaq', a 7-seater electric SUV with a cheaper price than Kia EV9 and IONIQ 9. It is a 7-seater electric SUV produced in Europe by a European manufacturer, and has secured price competitiveness compared to competing models. It is available in three variants and offers a range of up to more than 600 km (based on WLTP). It supports two-way charging (V2H) and V2L functions, enabling home power supply and use of external devices. Fable 5 was beating GPT 5.5 on every major benchmark. Then the US government pulled it offline. Anthropic's Fable 5 surpassed GPT 5.5 in major benchmarks, but the service was shut down three days after launch by order of the US government for security reasons. Fable 5 was the best-performing published AI model, outperforming GPT 5.5 by a wide margin in coding and inference benchmarks. On June 12, the U.S. government ordered Anthropic to shut down its service due to a jailbreak vulnerability discovered in Fable 5. The departure of its main competitor, Fable 5, makes GPT 5.5 the most powerful model currently available to developers and consumers. GM says its autonomous cars will eventually be capable of running as robotaxis too General Motors (GM) has advanced its autonomous driving technology and hinted at the possibility of expanding into the robotaxi business in the future. GM is taking a strategy to gradually expand the scope of autonomous driving applications, starting from highway driving to city centers. GM's chief product officer predicted that the business models of personal self-driving technology and robotaxi will eventually be integrated. In order to develop technology, we are re-employing former employees of 'Cruise', a former robotaxi division, and bringing in external experts to reassemble our technological capabilities. NHS England rolls out Microsoft 365 Copilot to 505,000 staff after trial reports 43 minutes saved per day NHS England has decided to introduce Microsoft 365 Copilot to 505,000 employees on a large scale after pilot testing proved its efficiency. As a result of a pilot operation with 30,000 people, we saved an average of 43 minutes of administrative work time per day per employee. This is the largest AI implementation in the medical field worldwide, with a contract worth approximately 120 million pounds signed. We plan to introduce it to all 505,000 people within the next year to reduce administrative burden and create an environment where we can focus on patient care. As Anthropic suspends access to new models, India debates its AI future Anthropic's decision to restrict access to cutting-edge AI models at the direction of the US government has reignited debate in India over the issue of technology dependence and the need to build 'sovereign AI'. Anthropic has been directed by the U.S. government to stop access to its latest AI models, Fable 5 and Mythos 5, to foreigners. The move shocked the AI ​​industry in India and again highlighted the risks of over-reliance on technology from certain US companies. Startups and investors in India are raising their voices for accelerating efforts to strengthen the country's AI capabilities and secure open source alternatives. Databricks Open-Sources Omnigent: A Meta-Harness That Composes, Governs, and Shares AI Agents Across Claude Code, Codex, and Pi Databricks has released 'Omnigent', an open-source meta-harness that enables integration, control, and sharing of various AI agents. Standardize individual AI agent harnesses such as existing Claude Code, Codex, and Pi into a common interface, making them interchangeable. It supports setting agent task policies and sharing real-time sessions through three core features: Composition, Control, and Collaboration. Built-in Omnibox sandbox restricts access to the operating system and safely protects sensitive information such as API tokens. GLM 5.2 released Zhipu has released GLM-5.2, the most powerful open source model that supports 1M context windows and can perform independent long-term tasks. GLM-5.2 is Zhipu's most powerful open source model with 1M context window and long-term task independent performance ability. In situations where non-technical access is restricted in certain frontier models, the openness and accessibility of intelligence is emphasized and provided to developers. It will be provided first to current GLM Coding Plan users (Lite/Pro/Max), and the API will be released next week. repo-slopscore: Detect AI/LLM contributions in Git repositories by analyzing commit history. Covers the functionality and critical perspectives of 'repo-slopscore', a tool that detects and scores AI and LLM contributions by analyzing the commit history of Git repositories. repo-slopscore is a service that automatically scans and scores AI/LLM contribution traces in open source projects by analyzing commit records. Supports repositories from various Git hosting platforms such as GitHub, Codeberg, and Bitbucket, and scans widely from known open source projects to security-related infrastructure repositories. The tool has been criticized for its harsh scoring method that does not take context into account, the vulnerability of its signals, and the encouragement of negative perceptions about projects using AI technology. A huge shadow cast over this Fable affair. An analysis of the situation in which foreign nationals' access to Anthropic's powerful AI models, Fable 5 and Mythos 5, was completely blocked due to export control orders from the U.S. government, and its ramifications. Based on national security authority, the U.S. government ordered Anthropic's Fable 5 and Mythos 5 models to be blocked from access by all foreign nationals inside and outside the United States. Anthropic countered that the jailbreak bypass vulnerability raised by the government was already known to be minor and could be found in other models. Doubts have been raised about whether this measure is actual AI safety regulation or political and competitive pressure targeting specific companies, and concerns have been raised about future declines in AI accessibility. Conversation between Amazon CEO and U.S. officials sparks crackdown on Anthropic models Following a conversation between Amazon's CEO and U.S. officials, the Trump administration blocked all overseas use of Anthropic's top AI model, citing cybersecurity concerns. Amazon researchers identified vulnerabilities that could be exploited for cyberattacks in Anthropic's 'Fable 5' model and delivered it to the U.S. government. Citing security concerns and political distrust, the Trump administration decided to completely block international user access to Anthropic's 'Mythos' and 'Fable' models. The move makes it virtually impossible for Anthropic's foreign researchers to work on cutting-edge models and deepens government control and political intervention in the AI ​​industry. Open source AI must win This article argues for the need for open source AI that guarantees operational freedom and technical independence so that AI infrastructure is not dependent on a few companies. AI is an essential infrastructure of modern civilization and must be free from the control of specific companies and can be freely researched, distributed, and modified. If intelligent systems are subordinated to a small number of closed platform companies, there is a risk that the ‘subscription economy of cognition’ will become entrenched. There is a spectrum of openness in open source models, including local feasibility and disclosure of learning data, and building a sustainable ecosystem is important. The Verifier Tax: Horizon-Dependent Safety–Success Tradeoffs in Tool-Using LLM Agents [R] This study analyzed the 'Verifier Tax', a trade-off phenomenon between task success rate and safety that occurs during the safety verification process when an LLM agent uses a tool. Successful work does not mean safety, and we analyzed the problem of 'unsafe success', which involves success while violating safety policies. We proposed a two-stage verification architecture that combines deterministic verification and LLM-based verification. We confirmed the 'Verifier Tax' phenomenon, where safety verification lowers the success rate of work as the work horizon becomes longer. Confused, where to start [D] Backend and big data developers want to start learning voice generation LLM skills, but are confused by too many learning materials and a curriculum that starts from scratch. The questioner has experience in backend and big data development. Want to study in the field of Speech Generation AI (LLM) Feeling confused at the starting point of learning due to materials starting from basic regression analysis The future of Siri, or: why private inference isn’t private enough A security discussion on how Apple's new AI-powered Siri works in conjunction with Google's model and infrastructure while protecting personal information. Apple plans to introduce Google's Gemini model to strengthen Siri's AI capabilities We use the 'Private Cloud Compute' (PCC) system to process personal data on users' devices, and extend this to Google's infrastructure. The core goal of PCC is to ensure that data is encrypted and deleted immediately after processing, ensuring that even Apple and Google cannot see your personal data. There is still controversy among security experts as to whether these 'extended' PCC systems are sufficiently secure from external threats. Before you buy a smartwatch or smart ring, consider what you're giving up Warns about the privacy and security risks of health data collected by wearable devices such as smartwatches and smart rings. Wearable devices collect sensitive data that goes beyond activity, including health, sleep, and reproductive health, but there is a lack of comprehensive federal regulation. There is a risk that the collected data may be leaked or sold to third parties for purposes of which the user is not aware, such as marketing or insurance profiling. HIPAA does not protect data collected by general wearable devices other than medical institutions, so users must check and manage their own privacy policies. I found the most effortless way to clean your Android phone storage - and it's free to use This article introduces the 'Sponge' app that can efficiently organize your Android phone's photo storage space. The Sponge app uses a Tinder-like swipe interface (delete left, stay right) to make deleting photos quick and easy. Users can utilize the function to delete photos individually or in bulk by date or collection. The app is basically free, but features for deleting videos or collections may require a fee. AWS Introduces Durable Storage Option for ElastiCache for Valkey AWS has introduced a durable storage option in ElastiCache for Valkey, enabling you to leverage persistent data workloads beyond caching. You can choose between synchronous mode, which prioritizes data loss prevention, and asynchronous mode, which maintains low latency. It can be used for various workloads that require permanent data storage, such as AI memory, session storage, and RAG knowledge base. Read latency is maintained in microseconds, and asynchronous mode provides a data loss buffer of up to 10 seconds. Hardware benchmark ‘AA-Agent Puff’ appears... Blackwell ranks first in power efficiency Artificial Analysis has unveiled a new hardware benchmark 'AA-AgentPerf' that evaluates inference performance and power efficiency based on actual AI agent workload. Beyond measuring simple query performance, hardware performance is evaluated by reproducing the complex workflow of the coding agent and the actual operating environment. By introducing 'number of agents per megawatt' as a key indicator, we adopted an evaluation method that simultaneously considers power efficiency and service quality. In the first test, the NVIDIA Blackwell (GB300) system recorded the highest power efficiency, and will be operated as a live benchmark with real-time updates. Artificial Analysis introduces ‘Deep SWE’ benchmark... ‘Fable 5’ ranks first in coding Artificial Analysis, an AI performance analysis agency, has revamped its coding agent performance rankings by introducing a new evaluation method 'Deep SWE' that complements the limitations of existing benchmarks. Artificial Analysis (AA) has adopted a new 'DeepSWE' benchmark to minimize the problem of exposing the model's pre-trained answer. The existing 'SWE-Bench Pro' was criticized for not accurately reflecting skill, as the model tracks commit records to provide the correct answer. As a result of the benchmark replacement, Claude Fable 5(max) ranked first with 77 points, followed by GPT-5.5-based codex with 76 points. The US State Government Association conducts a surprise investigation into Open AI... Protection of vulnerable groups and verification of technical defects A coalition of U.S. state attorneys general has launched a wide-ranging investigation into OpenAI's business model, technical flaws, and influence on vulnerable populations. A coalition of U.S. state attorneys general, including New York State, sent a subpoena to Open AI, requesting the submission of data. The scope of the investigation includes handling consumer data, countering model flattery, and marketing and influencing vulnerable groups. Cases where AI chatbots have been abused for social harm, such as crime or suicide, have become the background, and regulations on major AI companies, beyond Open AI, are being strengthened. [Ahn Kwang-seop's AI Truth-Thesis] The world's strongest AI pursued by the US government... Korea's alternative is This is an analysis of the incident in which the U.S. government forcibly suspended Antropic's latest AI models, 'Fable 5' and 'Missos 5', worldwide in the name of export control. On June 12, 2026, under the order of U.S. Secretary of Commerce Howard Rutnick, Antropic's AI models 'Fable 5' and 'Missos 5' were immediately shut down worldwide to block access by foreigners. Unlike past hardware export controls, this measure remotely 'turns off' the software model itself through API, showing that the subject of national security and export control has moved from atoms to bits. Antropic objected, saying that the jailbreak vulnerability was similar to that of other models, but it stopped providing the model in accordance with mandatory guidelines from the U.S. government, forcing API users to switch infrastructure. Association of U.S. Attorneys General launches comprehensive investigation into Open AI... Regulatory pressure on the AI ​​industry reaches its peak Attorneys general from 42 U.S. states have joined forces to launch a comprehensive joint investigation into Open AI's technical side effects and data management methods. A coalition of attorneys general from 42 U.S. states issued a subpoena to OpenAI and demanded that it submit extensive internal data. Investigations include advertising and user engagement practices, data handling, and activities with minors and older adults. Coinciding with the timing of Open AI's initial public offering (IPO), it is expected to act as a significant variable in the future listing process and investment sentiment."